.TH TUIDESK\-CONFIG 5 2026-10-27 "tuidesk 0.1.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
tuidesk\-config \- tuidesk configuration file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tuidesk/config.toml
.br
.I ~/.config/tuidesk/config.toml
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR tuidesk (1)
reads its settings from a TOML file.
The file is created with every option and a comment on first start, and it is reloaded
whenever it is saved.
The values in the file are merged over the built\-in defaults
.RB ( "tuidesk \-\-print\-config" ),
so a file only needs the keys that differ.
Tables are merged key by key; any other value, including an array, replaces the default.
.PP
System Settings (prefix key, then
.BR S )
edits the common options with a live preview and saves them into this file, keeping its
comments and layout.
.PP
Colors are written as
.BR \(dq#rrggbb\(dq ,
a name such as
.B \(dqblue\(dq
or
.BR \(dqlightblue\(dq ,
a 0\-255 palette index, or
.BR \(dqreset\(dq .
Paths may start with
.BR ~ .
.SH GENERAL
The
.B [general]
table.
.TP
.BR shell " (string, default \(dq\(dq)"
Shell for new terminal windows.
Empty means
.BR $SHELL ,
then
.BR /bin/sh .
.TP
.BR prefix " (key, default \(dqctrl+space\(dq)"
The prefix key for window manager commands; see
.BR KEYS .
.TP
.BR layout " (default \(dqfloating\(dq)"
Initial layout of each desktop:
.B floating
(windows go where you put them), or a tiled one:
.B master
(master and stack),
.B monocle
(one window at a time),
.BR grid ,
.B columns
or
.B bsp
(binary splits).
.TP
.BR master_ratio " (0.1\-0.9, default 0.55)"
Share of the width used by the master window in tiled layouts.
.TP
.BR gaps " (cells, default 0)"
Gap between tiled windows.
.TP
.BR scrollback " (lines, default 5000)"
History kept per window.
.TP
.BR color_mode " (default \(dqauto\(dq)"
.BR auto ,
.BR truecolor ,
.B 256
or
.BR 16 .
Use
.B 16
on the Linux console.
.TP
.BR window_width ", " window_height " (percent, default 70)"
Size of new floating windows, relative to the desktop.
.TP
.BR close_on_exit " (bool, default true)"
Close a window when its program exits.
.TP
.BR focus_follows_mouse " (bool, default false)"
Focus the window under the pointer without clicking.
.TP
.BR dim_inactive " (bool, default false)"
Dim the content of unfocused windows.
.TP
.BR notification_timeout " (seconds, default 5)"
How long a notification popup stays.
.TP
.BR hide_missing_apps " (bool, default true)"
Leave launcher entries out when their program is not found on
.BR $PATH .
.TP
.BR builtin_apps " (bool, default true)"
Include the built\-in catalogue of common terminal programs in the launcher; see
.BR APPS .
.TP
.BR hidden_apps " (array of names, default [])"
Launcher entries to leave out, matched by name without regard to case.
.TP
.BR autostart " (array of commands, default [])"
Commands opened in windows when a server starts without a saved session.
.TP
.BR desktops " (1\-9, default 4)"
Number of virtual desktops.
.TP
.BR desktop_names " (array of strings, default [])"
Names shown in the pager and when switching; empty entries show the number.
.TP
.BR restore_session " (bool, default true)"
Save open windows and reopen them on the next start.
.TP
.BR inherit_cwd " (bool, default true)"
New windows start in the focused window's directory.
.TP
.BR images " (bool, default true)"
Show images that programs send with the kitty graphics, Sixel or iTerm2 protocols.
.TP
.BR image_protocol " (default \(dqauto\(dq)"
How images reach the host terminal:
.B auto
(detect),
.B kitty
(Unicode placeholders: kitty, Ghostty),
.B iterm
(iTerm2, WezTerm, VS Code),
.B sixel
(foot, xterm, Konsole) or
.BR none .
.TP
.BR pixel_buttons " (bool, default true)"
Draw the title bar buttons
.B [_] [^] [x]
as icons when the terminal shows images (needs
.BR images ).
.SH THEME
The
.B [theme]
table.
.TP
.BR preset " (default \(dqbreeze\-dark\(dq)"
.BR breeze\-dark ,
.B breeze\-light
or
.B tty16
(16 colors, for the Linux console).
.TP
.B border
Window border style:
.BR plain ,
.BR rounded ,
.BR double ,
.B thick
or
.BR ascii .
.PP
Any of these colors overrides the preset:
.BR accent ,
.BR wallpaper ,
.BR wallpaper_fg ,
.BR panel_bg ,
.BR panel_fg ,
.BR task_active_bg ,
.BR task_active_fg ,
.BR title_active_bg ,
.BR title_active_fg ,
.BR title_inactive_bg ,
.BR title_inactive_fg ,
.BR border_active ,
.BR border_inactive ,
.BR term_bg ,
.BR term_fg ,
.BR menu_bg ,
.BR menu_fg ,
.BR menu_dim ,
.BR menu_sel_bg ,
.BR menu_sel_fg ,
.BR notif_bg ,
.BR notif_fg ,
.BR urgent ,
.BR button_close .
.SH PANEL
The
.B [panel]
table.
.TP
.BR position " (default \(dqbottom\(dq)"
.B bottom
or
.BR top .
.TP
.B widgets
Panel widgets in order.
Widgets before
.B tasks
are aligned left, those after it right.
Built in:
.BR kickoff ,
.BR pager ,
.BR tasks ,
.BR layout ,
.BR cpu ,
.BR mem ,
.BR battery ,
.BR bell ,
.BR clock .
A Lua widget registered as
.I name
is written
.BI lua: name\fR.
.TP
.BR kickoff_label " (default \(dq tuidesk \(dq)"
Text of the launcher button.
.TP
.BR clock_format " (default \(dq%a %d %b  %H:%M\(dq)"
.BR strftime (3)
format of the clock.
.SH WALLPAPER
.BI [wallpaper. n ]
for desktop
.I n
(1\-9), over
.B [wallpaper.default]
for all desktops.
.TP
.B kind
.B logo
(default: the logo and key hints),
.B none
(plain color),
.B art
(ASCII art),
.B pattern
.RB ( text
repeated over the desktop) or
.B lua
(text from a Lua widget).
.TP
.BR color ", " fg
Background and text color, over the theme's.
.TP
.B text
The art or the repeated pattern.
.TP
.B file
A file with the art.
.TP
.B widget
The Lua widget for
.BR lua .
.TP
.B position
Where art is placed:
.B center
(default),
.BR top\-left ,
.BR top ,
.BR top\-right ,
.BR left ,
.BR right ,
.BR bottom\-left ,
.BR bottom ,
.BR bottom\-right .
.SH DESKTOP WIDGETS
Each
.B [[desktop_widgets]]
entry is drawn on the wallpaper, under the windows.
.TP
.B kind
.B clock
(a big clock and the date),
.B notes
(a text file; click it to edit it in
.BR $EDITOR ),
.B sysinfo
(CPU, memory and battery bars) or
.B lua
(text from a Lua widget).
.TP
.BR position " (default \(dqtop\-right\(dq)"
As for wallpaper art.
.TP
.B desktops
Array of 1\-based desktops to show on; all when omitted.
.TP
.BR title ", " file ", " widget ", " format
The heading, the notes file, the Lua widget, and the
.BR strftime (3)
format of a clock (default
.BR \(dq%H:%M\(dq ).
.TP
.BR width ", " height
Size in cells instead of the automatic one.
.SH SCREENSHOT
The
.B [screenshot]
table.
.TP
.BR dir " (default \(dq~/Pictures/tuidesk\(dq)"
Where screenshots are saved, as
.BI tuidesk\- YYYYmmdd\-HHMMSS\-mmm . format\fR.
.TP
.BR format " (default \(dqhtml\(dq)"
.B txt
(plain text),
.B ansi
(colored text for
.B cat
or
.BR "less \-R" ),
.B html
or
.BR svg .
.TP
.BR copy " (default \(dqpath\(dq)"
What to copy to the clipboard after saving:
.BR path ,
.B text
or
.BR none .
.SH KEYS
.B [keys.prefix]
maps keys pressed after the prefix key to actions, and
.B [keys.global]
maps keys caught directly, before the focused program sees them.
Keys are written like
.BR ctrl+space ,
.BR alt+shift+tab ,
.BR f5 ,
.B enter
or a single character, where
.B T
means shift+t.
The action
.B none
turns a default binding off.
.PP
Actions:
.BR kickoff ,
.BR spawn_shell ,
.BI spawn " command" ,
.BI launch " app name" ,
.BR close ,
.BR maximize ,
.BR minimize ,
.BR focus_next ,
.BR focus_prev ,
.BR switcher ,
.BR switcher_prev ,
.BR tile_left ,
.BR tile_right ,
.BR tile_top ,
.BR tile_bottom ,
.BR toggle_layout ,
.BR cycle_layout ,
.BI layout " name" ,
.BR toggle_floating ,
.BR swap_master ,
.BR window_mode ,
.BR scroll_up ,
.BR scroll_down ,
.BI desktop " n" ,
.BR desktop_next ,
.BR desktop_prev ,
.BI move_to_desktop " n" ,
.BR move_next_desktop ,
.BR move_prev_desktop ,
.BR paste ,
.BR copy_mode ,
.BR clipboard ,
.BR help ,
.BR window_menu ,
.BR toggle_above ,
.BR rename ,
.BR rename_desktop ,
.BR runner ,
.BR overview ,
.BR screenshot ,
.BR "screenshot window" ,
.BR "screenshot region" ,
.BR notifications ,
.BR settings ,
.BR detach ,
.BR reload ,
.BR quit ,
.BI lua " function"
(call a global Lua function).
The default bindings are listed in
.BR tuidesk (1).
.SH APPS
The launcher (Kickoff and the runner) lists a built\-in catalogue of about 40 well\-known
terminal programs
.RB ( "tuidesk \-\-print\-apps" ),
showing only those that are installed.
Each
.B [[apps]]
entry is added to it; an entry with the same name as a built\-in one replaces it.
.TP
.B name
Shown in the launcher, and used by
.BI launch " name"\fR.
.TP
.B command
Run through
.BR /bin/sh ,
so arguments and pipes work.
.TP
.BR category " (default \(dqOther\(dq)"
The launcher tab it appears under.
.TP
.B description
Shown next to the name.
.SH RULES
Each
.B [[rules]]
entry applies to new windows whose command's first word equals
.B command
and/or whose title contains
.BR title .
Window titles start as the launcher entry's name.
.TP
.BR width ", " height
Size in percent of the desktop.
.TP
.BR x ", " y
Position in cells.
.TP
.BR maximized ", " minimized ", " floating ", " above
Booleans;
.B above
keeps the window on top of others.
.TP
.B desktop
1\-based desktop to open on, without switching to it.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
[general]
layout = "master"
desktops = 6
desktop_names = ["Main", "Code", "Web", "Chat"]
hidden_apps = ["Python"]

[theme]
preset = "breeze\-light"
accent = "#ff8800"
border = "rounded"

[panel]
position = "top"

[keys.prefix]
"g" = "launch Git"
"v" = "spawn nvim ~/notes.md"

[[apps]]
name = "Notes"
command = "nvim ~/notes.md"
category = "Office"

[[rules]]
command = "htop"
maximized = true
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tuidesk/config.toml
This file; another directory can be given with
.BR "tuidesk \-c" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tuidesk (1),
.BR tuidesk\-lua (7)
